 1427 2ABA
 1428 2ABA              ; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
 1429 2ABA              ; binary32: float arithmetic, comparison and conversions to and from long.
 1430 2ABA              ;
 1431 2ABA              ; The compiler calls these for every float operation: a float is its bits, an operand like a
 1432 2ABA              ; long -- a in HL (low word) and DE (high word), b in BC (low) and on the stack above the return
 1433 2ABA              ; address (high), left there for the caller to take off -- and the result in HL:DE, a comparison's
 1434 2ABA              ; in A. The algorithms are those of the compiler's C reference implementation of IEEE 754, and the
 1435 2ABA              ; results agree with it bit for bit: one rounding, to the nearest with ties to even; subnormals;
 1436 2ABA              ; infinities; and NaNs that come back quieted, the first operand's when both are, as on the
 1437 2ABA              ; x86.
 1438 2ABA              ;
 1439 2ABA              ; A finite number in the middle of an operation is a sign (in fps), an exponent in BC and a
 1440 2ABA              ; significand of thirty-two bits in DEHL, D the top byte, its leading one at bit 31: twenty-four
 1441 2ABA              ; bits of the result and eight below them, which decide the rounding -- the round bit is bit 7,
 1442 2ABA              ; and whatever was shifted out below bit 0 is kept as a one in bit 0, the sticky bit. Its value is
 1443 2ABA              ; DEHL / 2^31 * 2^(BC - 127), so BC is the biased exponent the result has before rounding.
 1444 2ABA              ; __x80_fp_rpack makes the float of that. The operands wait in fpa and fpb, the bytes as in
 1445 2ABA              ; memory, low first.
 1446 2ABA              ;
 1447 2ABA              ; Not reentrant: an interrupt handler doing float arithmetic while the main program is inside one
