 1896 2ABA ~            ; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
 1897 2ABA ~            ; DE:HL = a * b. The product of the twenty-four-bit significands, a2 a1 a0 by b2 b1 b0, forty-eight
 1898 2ABA ~            ; bits, bytes 5 to 0, is made of five of __x80_mul8w's, a byte by a word: a0, a1 and a2 by b's low
 1899 2ABA ~            ; word, b2 by a's, and a2 by b2, each added in where it belongs as it comes, in registers. Its top
 1900 2ABA ~            ; thirty-two bits are the result's significand, bytes 1 and 0 only its sticky bit -- after a shift
 1901 2ABA ~            ; by one when the leading one is at bit 46 rather than 47. A product with a zero byte or word is
 1902 2ABA ~            ; zero and not made: a number with a short significand -- 4.0, 10.0, 0.5, most constants -- needs
 1903 2ABA ~            ; two of the five or three.
 1904 2ABA ~            ; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
 1905 2ABA ~            __x80_fmul:
 1906 2ABA ~                IFDEF X80_OPT_SIZE
