 5910 2C1A              ; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
 5911 2C1A              ; L = L shifted by E, the three shifts of a byte, for a count the compiler knows
 5912 2C1A              ; is below eight -- `128 >> (x & 7)` made a byte (ivagor, zx-pk.ru), which was
 5913 2C1A              ; the word shifted by __x80_ashr16. The byte is in L as the word's low byte was,
 5914 2C1A              ; so that A stays free around the call; A and E are spent, BC, D and H are not.
 5915 2C1A              ; A count of zero is tested first, `XOR A / OR E / RET Z`, and the loop's test is
 5916 2C1A              ; at its end: a byte and 17 T-states less than counting down from one more, and 19
 5917 2C1A              ; T-states for no shift at all (ivagor, zx-pk.ru).
 5918 2C1A              ; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
