 6170 2C1A              ; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
 6171 2C1A              ; memcpy, memset and memmove of a length the program has only when it runs
 6172 2C1A              ; (lib/libc/string.c): HL = destination, DE = source (E the byte for memset),
 6173 2C1A              ; BC = the length; HL comes back as it went in, and A, BC, DE and the flags are
 6174 2C1A              ; written. Two bytes a trip, as __x80_mcpyp_even below (SIA, zx-pk.ru), the
 6175 2C1A              ; trips worked out here: one less than them is (n - 1) / 2 for an odd n and an
 6176 2C1A              ; even one alike, and the bit shifted out says which -- an odd n goes in at the
 6177 2C1A              ; second byte of the first pair. That halved, C its low byte and B its high one
 6178 2C1A              ; and each one more is what DEC C / JP NZ inside DEC B / JP NZ counts down. 0 is
 6179 2C1A              ; nothing at all, 65535 32768 trips. 31.5 T-states a byte for a copy and 19.5
 6180 2C1A              ; for a fill, against 39 and 27 for the loops in C they replace. -Os: a byte a
 6181 2C1A              ; trip, the length as the two counters straight away -- as fast as those loops
 6182 2C1A              ; were, and some ten bytes shorter each.
 6183 2C1A              ; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
 6184 2C1A              ; memmove: forwards by __x80_mcpyn when the destination is below the source,
 6185 2C1A              ; else from the last byte down. Ahead of __x80_mcpyn, so that its IFUSED has seen
 6186 2C1A              ; the jump to it.
 6187 2C1A              ;
 6188 2C1A              ; -mstack-copy: a long one through SP too, when the two are far enough apart that
 6189 2C1A              ; what an interrupt pushes cannot reach a byte still wanted (SIA, zx-pk.ru). Above
 6190 2C1A              ; the source by X80_SP_RESERVE + 16 or more, from the end down as memcpy goes,
 6191 2C1A              ; __x80_mcpys: an interrupt writes into the destination below SP, not yet written
 6192 2C1A              ; and above every byte of the source still to be read; and the first bytes, which
 6193 2C1A              ; it copies upwards at the end, are below what the source gave for the rest. Below
 6194 2C1A              ; it by X80_SP_RESERVE or more, upwards by __x80_mmoves, below.
 6195 2C1A                  IFUSED __x80_mmoven
