 6294 2C1A ~                IFUSED __x80_mmoves
 6295 2C1A ~            ; -mstack-copy, memmove upwards: the destination d below the source s by g = s - d, X80_SP_RESERVE
 6296 2C1A ~            ; or more, n at least X80_SP_RESERVE + 32. The first X80_SP_RESERVE to + 15 bytes the ordinary way;
 6297 2C1A ~            ; then SP the source's pointer, up from where they ended, HL the destination's, two bytes a POP --
 6298 2C1A ~            ; 34 T-states a pair, sixteen bytes a trip -- as far as the destination's end, d + n; then the last
 6299 2C1A ~            ; g bytes the ordinary way. Below SP is then always source already read that is destination not
 6300 2C1A ~            ; yet written: what an interrupt pushes lands there and is written over. Past d + n the source is
 6301 2C1A ~            ; the caller's still, and no interrupt may write it (ivagor, zx-pk.ru): there SP does not go. With
 6302 2C1A ~            ; fewer than X80_SP_RESERVE + 32 bytes up to there, all of it the ordinary way; apart, as memcpy.
 6303 2C1A ~            __x80_mmoves:
